PeakPack patch for pp2 (optional/ until pp2 is built; then listed in ../series and PP_REVISION=2).
ncrypt: import ECDSA keys (P-256/P-384/P-521, public and private blobs) through bcrypt.

.NET's ECDsa (PeakPack's mod-list signature check) imports the public key with NCryptImportKey,
using a generic "ECDP" BCRYPT_ECCPUBLIC_BLOB plus an NCRYPTBUFFER_ECC_CURVE_NAME ("nistP256")
parameter. Wine's ncrypt only imported RSA blobs and rejected every parameter list
(NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED), so verification failed under Wine. This accepts the curve-name parameter,
the specific ECS1..ECS6 magics and the generic ECDP/ECDV magics, maps generic blobs to the curve's
magic, imports through BCRYPT_ECDSA_P{256,384,521}_ALG_HANDLE, and gives the key object ECDSA
properties (Algorithm Group ECDSA, Length, signature length, ECCCurveName). Verification already
goes through NCryptVerifySignature -> BCryptVerifySignature. Other parameter buffer types are
still rejected.

Tested: Wine's ncrypt.c (original and patched) built as ncrypt.dll and run under
testkit/probes/cng_ecdsa_probe.c on Windows 10: original ncrypt_specific=FAIL (0x80090027),
ncrypt_dotnet=FAIL (0x80090029); patched both ok, tampered signature 0x80090006 (NTE_BAD_SIGNATURE).
Candidate for upstreaming to WineHQ.
Generated against CrossOver 26.3.0 sources/wine. Apply with: patch -p1 -d src/wine < this file

